# Build-context exclusions for the Dockerfile (MIGRATION_PLAN.md §6).
#
# Two jobs. The obvious one is keeping the context small -- the daemon tars
# everything not listed here and ships it before the build starts. The one that
# actually matters is making it structurally impossible to bake local machine
# state into a published image: a real database, a .env with live credentials,
# or a host-built node_modules.
#
# Note what is deliberately NOT excluded: frontend/ source (stage 1 builds it)
# and requirements.txt (stage 2 installs from it). Both are required inputs.

# --- VCS and tooling -------------------------------------------------------
.git
.gitignore
.gitattributes
.github
.claude
.vscode
.idea
**/.pytest_cache

# --- Python bytecode and local virtualenvs ---------------------------------
# The image installs its own dependencies for its own platform; a host .venv is
# both useless here and large.
**/__pycache__
**/*.pyc
**/*.pyo
.venv
.venv_new

# --- Node ------------------------------------------------------------------
# Excluded so `npm ci` installs the locked tree for the image's own platform
# (a Windows or macOS node_modules carries native binaries that cannot run in
# the container) and `npm run build` produces dist fresh rather than copying
# whatever stale bundle a host build happened to leave behind.
**/node_modules
frontend/dist
frontend/dist-ssr

# --- Local runtime state ---------------------------------------------------
# The Dockerfile copies no part of data/ at all, so these are belt-and-braces
# against a future COPY widening: a baked pawpal.db would ship one developer's
# pets and health records to every container started from the image. The -wal
# and -shm siblings matter as much as the .db itself -- storage.py runs the
# connection in WAL mode, so recent writes live in those files.
data/*.db
data/*.db-wal
data/*.db-shm
logs/*.log
logs/*.log.*
streamlit_run.log

# --- Secrets ---------------------------------------------------------------
# .env.example is re-included: it carries no values, only the documented list
# of variables.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# --- Docs and other non-runtime assets -------------------------------------
# Nothing here is imported by the server. The image's selective COPYs already
# keep tests/ and evaluation/ out of the final layers, so those stay in the
# context and remain available to a future build stage that wants to run them.
*.md
docs
diagrams
